 4. ☀️ Record tick summer 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Rebecca Zisser/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 This year's tick season has been a doozy — and another peak is coming in the fall, Axios' Carly Mallenbaum reports. 

 Why it matters: Tick bites can pose serious health risks, transmitting pathogens that cause illnesses including Lyme disease and triggering alpha-gal syndrome , an allergy to red meat. 🏥 By the numbers: August has had the highest rate of emergency department visits for tick bites since the CDC's tracker began in 2017, a major year for ticks.

 That comes after a record-breaking April . Share this story . 

 
 
